My first Amiga was a A500 in 1988, I remember it cost
about 4.4 times the monthly rent, it was definitely  
not cheap in any means but it had power like nothing 
else                                                 

I had really fun with it and my aim is to have that  
replicated with my "A500" build                      

I owned A500, A600, A1200, A4000, A4000T, A1200      
                     |                |              
                     ------ CD32 ------              

The last A1200 was the Escom one and sold it 2007

Recent years...

mini Walker, THEA500 Mini, A600GS, Apollo V4    

and... only mini Walker is still in my collection

Soon I will have a new one, THE A1200 and it will all
be fun again, aesthetics is very important thing     

I also have my A1200.net case with a A500 keyboard in
it and thats how far it has come, everything is so   
expensive, now that BigMig is in development and it  
feels appealing, fast 68k with 3D maybe put that one 
in the A1200 case ;)                                 



