@node "AT97" "AmiTech97"
@{JCENTER}@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/32seonliner.png"}

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/a97.png"}

AmiTech 97 was a prominent, dedicated Amiga computer exposition 
and computer party held in Stockholm, Sweden in April 1997. 
Organized during a period of massive grassroots enthusiasm for 
the Amiga platform, the event served as a major gathering hub 
for the Scandinavian Amiga tech scene and the regional Demoscene.

Major Amiga retailers and tech companies such as Micsam participated
in the event to showcase software packages, hardware expansions, and
protoypes to an enthusiastic user base

The event hosted competitive "computer party" tournaments where 
creators submitted demos.

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/amitech1.jpg"}
1th place, 1997-04-26 Amitech by Tulou

@{" Unpack " SYSTEM "c:execute demo"}

Requires WHDL installed, only exits when demo done



I was actually at AmiTech 97 with my company Micsam at that time,
this is truly lost times. Background is Micsam data booth
Company was registered Micsam, "data" was added in showcase materials

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/amitech97.png"}
This is me, 29 years ago! screenshot from YouTube, want to see the
video search for "AmiTech 97 ACG Amiga"


I even met Petro Tyschtschenko and had a small chat, the Pontiac was
at the entrance to AmiTech 97 and was "shown" to me by Riku Bergquist,
can't remember if it was his car... think it was.

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/pontiac.jpeg"}


